; One binary, two names. As dinput8.dll only DirectInput8Create is ever asked for; a copy renamed to
; d3d9.dll - which is how the mod loads on Proton without a launch option - is asked for the Direct3D
; entry points instead. Exporting both sets costs nothing and keeps the two installs on one build.
;
; PSGPError, PSGPSampleTexture, DebugSetMute, DebugSetLevel, Direct3DShaderValidatorCreate9 and
; Direct3D9EnableMaximizedWindowedModeShim are deliberately absent: they are undocumented, nothing
; outside the Direct3D debug runtime imports them by name, and a wrong guess at an argument count
; would corrupt the caller's stack rather than fail cleanly.

EXPORTS
    DirectInput8Create

    Direct3DCreate9
    Direct3DCreate9Ex
    D3DPERF_BeginEvent
    D3DPERF_EndEvent
    D3DPERF_GetStatus
    D3DPERF_QueryRepeatFrame
    D3DPERF_SetMarker
    D3DPERF_SetOptions
    D3DPERF_SetRegion
